Treat the guesses as ONE evolving attempt at the same fixed answer, not as separate questions. The
answer never changes; only the player understanding of it does. Drawing notes describe what was
visible at the time of each guess, interpreted in relation to the answer - use them as extra
context, for example where the drawing pointed toward a category or association the guesses did
not line up with. If no drawing note is given, work only from the description and synonyms. Do not
pad the note to produce a separate point for every guess: if several guesses are substantively
similar, one point covering them all is correct.
